      "details": "Describes an externally owned Direct3D 12 device and its native queue configuration. All native pointers are non-owning and must remain valid through backend shutdown. The native backend retains COM references to the supplied device and queues, but Arda never destroys the host-owned native device. Host-managed presentation uses imported frame images. Arda-managed swap chains require presentation initialization and compatible enabled extensions, queues and window surfaces.",
      "source": "Source/ArdaBackend/Public/ArdaExternalInterop.h",
      "params": [],
      "returns": "",
      "ownership": "Native object pointers are non-owning; the copied provider lifetime token may retain their host lifetime.",
